# Card packing

A horizontal row of cards must fill 100% of the content width. Do not leave an empty track to the right of the last card (Favorites Wales is the example). If a row would end short, place one or two sibling cards that fit the leftover width, or let the last-row items grow so the row stays full.

Cards in the same row share one height. A short text fact next to a taller neighbor stretches to that height. Title stays top-left. Number and description pin to the bottom-left.

Do not stretch one text-only fact beside a tall story card. Put two or three facts in a stack on the right instead. A chart card (dots / mix-chart) keeps the fact on the title; leftover height goes to the chart, sized to that stack (usually two facts).

Story cards with circles (Zidane): hug the content. Circles sit on one horizontal row at the bottom. Do not stretch empty space under the circles. Drop the sibling fact if it forces the story card taller than its graphic.

Inner inset on every card is `--size-card-pad` (`space/l`, 20px). Do not mix `l` and `xl` on card edges.

On viewports ≤900px, Home story cards stay in reading order. Fact stacks move to the bottom of the page so the screen is not a long vertical list of Barcelona/Zidane facts.

Do not fade or slide the chrome when switching routes. Tab changes must not flicker.
